            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0254" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/487: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-24T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1927—noon.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 24—6:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>244. The following from American consul at Nanking.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Approximately 175 women and children were evacuated yesterday. Fourteen
                        women and sixteen children were sent to Shanghai by steamer <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pi Yang</hi>. Remainder are being cared for on board
                        the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">W. B. Preston</hi> and U. S. S. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Noa.</hi></p>
                    <p>Cantonese troops have entered the city. A small naval guard has been
                        established at this consulate.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
